  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Safe and Responsible Sport in African Sport - Region 5</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building and monitoring a regional approach toward a standard of rights based, safe, inclusive and responsible sport structures, systems and programs. 

The overall NIF project&#x2019;s primary objective is to enhance opportunities for marginalized persons to benefit from and participate in sports. For to achieve this, NIF focuses on 1) To build lasting partnerships and networks to gain sustainable organizations that deliver safe, equitable and inclusive sports activities, 2) To enhance management resources in the development of inclusive and equitable partner programs with resources, and 3) Strengthened capacity of sports organizations to implement safe, equitable and inclusive sport. Emphasis is on the inclusion of women and girls, children/youth, persons with disabilities, and refugees. Implementation in Malawi, Zambia, and Zimbabwe.</narrative>
  </description>
